      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Fort Selden was established in 1865 in an effort to bring peace to a region besieged by desperado attacks and Indian raids that impeded dreams of US expansion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newmexico.org/places-to-visit/regions/southwest/radium-springs-fort-selden/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Radium Springs once hosted a popular health retreat in the early 1900s, drawing visitors to its mineral-rich hot springs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newmexico.org/places-to-visit/regions/southwest/radium-springs-fort-selden/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Dripping Springs Resort, built in 1916, was a lavish spa that now stands as a historic ruin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newmexico.org/places-to-visit/regions/southwest/radium-springs-fort-selden/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Radium Springs is home to the Leasburg Dam, a distinctive water control structure on the Rio Grande.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newmexico.org/places-to-visit/regions/southwest/radium-springs-fort-selden/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Across the Rio Grande from Radium Springs lies the Rio Grande Bridge and the ruins of 19th‑century Fort Selden.",
